#! /bin/sh
# Sleep at each point where grep's threads hand data over to each other
# (GREP_TEST_DELAY sites in src/grep.c, honored by the test builds
# src/grep-hooks and src/grep-shrunk), one point at a time, so that the
# other threads run ahead into the window.  A thread that still uses an
# object that another may free or reuse, a wakeup that can be missed,
# or an exit that races with running workers then shows up as different
# output, a crash, a sanitizer report, or a hang.
#
